 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Their claim «افتراه» is framed («المكذبون به عنادًا وبغيًا»). The destruction of past nations (39:15-19) is not glossed or drawn. 41 is the Prophet's ﷺ words: no motif. A book for «القرآن» and «تفصيل الكتاب», an hourglass for «ولما يأتهم تأويله», two paths for «ومنهم من يؤمن به ومنهم من لا يؤمن به». STAGING v4: c1 (37-38) stays ambient: the Quran's origin and the challenge to bring a sura like it (38:4-16 are the Prophet's commanded words: quiet). Plates: a book for the Quran (37:4), a scroll for the earlier scriptures it confirms (37:11), a book for the detailing of the Book (37:15). c2 (39-40) is staged in a town by day: three deniers (dark robes) walk in on 39:1 and shake their heads under a book plate on 39:2-3 (they hastened to deny the Quran before understanding it, Al-Muyassar); an hourglass for what it promised that has not yet come (39:7); the earlier nations and their end are not drawn: on 39:15-19 (addressed to the Prophet) the camera only closes on the deniers. On 40:1 three believers (some of them believe in it) appear sitting and read on 40:3, while the deniers shake their heads on 40:7 (some do not); the threat 40:10-12 keeps the camera on the deniers. c3 (41) stays ambient: the Prophet's commanded words, quiet over 41:3-15. The cover now shows the book plate (37:5)."
 },
